## 🎯 Overview

&gt; Most image enhancement systems stop at GPU inference. **This project doesn't.**

The entire pipeline is designed around **FPGA deployment**, **low-latency inference**, and **hardware-aware optimization**. From Quantization-Aware Training (QAT) to Vitis AI compilation and DPU execution, every stage is built with embedded Edge AI deployment in mind.

### What it does
| Task | Status |
|------|--------|
| 🔅 Low-light restoration | ✅ |
| 🌫️ Denoising | ✅ |
| 🔍 Blur reduction | ✅ |
| ⚡ Efficient INT8 inference | ✅ |
| 🚀 Hardware-accelerated deployment | ✅ |

**No TensorRT. No GPU dependency.** Built specifically for FPGA acceleration pipelines.

---

## ✨ Features

| Component | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Deep Learning Model** | Residual CNN architecture |
| **Quantization** | INT8 Quantization-Aware Training |
| **FPGA Workflow** | Xilinx Vitis AI deployment |
| **Hardware Acceleration** | DPU inference engine |
| **Enhancement Tasks** | Denoising, low-light enhancement, deblurring |
| **Evaluation** | PSNR & SSIM metrics |
| **Deployment** | Docker-based runtime |
| **Target Platform** | FPGA Edge AI systems |

---

## 📁 Project Structure
FPGA-Image-Enhancement/
├── 📂 models/              # Trained & quantized models
├── 📂 testing_code/        # Inference & evaluation scripts
├── 📂 testing_images/      # Sample input images
├── 📂 output/              # Enhanced output images
├── 📂 results/             # Benchmark & evaluation outputs
├── 📂 docs/                # Technical documentation
├── Dockerfile
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md


